// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row box_deref_move_refused_outside_let (tier 3, `refuses`).
// MOVING THE BOXED VALUE OUT OF A `Box` IS LOWERED AT THE `let` RHS AND NOWHERE
// ELSE.
//
// Legal Rust: `Box` is the one type with DerefMove, so `eat(*b)` moves the boxed
// value into the callee. TODAY: "cannot move out of a value behind a reference /
// out of an index (E0507)".
//
// ROOT, by symbol: `try_lower_box_deref_move` (src/compiler/sema_stmt.cpp) has ONE
// call site — the RHS of `lower_let`:
//     rhs = try_lower_box_deref_move(rhs_node);
//     if (!rhs) rhs = lower_expr(rhs_node);
// and the comment beside the E0507 that follows it names the gap outright: "raw-ptr
// deref/index, Box deref-move, Vec-index (method-deref), field-out-of-self, and
// return/arg positions are NOT caught here". Every other value position runs
// `is_unowned_move_source` with no Box exemption. Measured, one program per
// position on this binary: the `let` position COMPILES and drops once (lattice
// f_box_deref_move_in_let_ctl, count 1), the RETURN position compiles
// (f_box_deref_move_in_return, count 1), the ARGUMENT position is refused (this
// program, and c_move_out_of_box) and the STRUCT-LITERAL FIELD position is refused
// with a second sentence, "cannot move out of a value behind a shared reference
// (E0507)" (f_box_deref_move_in_ctor).
//
// ⚠ THE OTHER HALF OF THIS PROPERTY IS ALREADY ROWED AND IT FAILS THE OTHER WAY:
// `box_field_move` moves a FIELD out of a Box, is ADMITTED, and double-frees
// (lattice cell c_move_field_out_of_box reads count 2 where Rust reads 1). One
// helper answers "may this Box be moved through" and three positions consume the
// answer; the refusal and the double free are two roots, not one, and the grouping
// was tested by asking whether one candidate change moves both — it does not: this
// one is in the move classifier, that one in codegen.
// Rust: compiles, exit 0.
package box_deref_move_refused_outside_let;
use logos.mem.boxed;
struct D { v: i64, c: *mut i64 }
impl Drop for D { fn drop(self: &mut D) { unsafe { *self.c = *self.c + self.v; } } }
fn eatd(x: D) -> i64 { return x.v; }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut n: i64 = 0i64;
    let p: *mut i64 = &mut n;
    let mut r: i64 = 0i64;
    {
        let b: Box<D> = Box::new(D { v: 1i64, c: p });
        r = eatd(*b);
    }
    if r != 1i64 { return 2i32; }
    let got: i64 = unsafe { n };
    if got != 1i64 { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
